  description="A Rust library for building terminal user interfaces."
>
  <p>
    Wove lays out a tree of elements in terminal cells, handles keyboard and
    mouse input, and renders changes to the screen.
  </p>

  <h2 id="choose-how-to-build">Choose how to build</h2>
  <ul class="overview-links">
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/start/">Rust core</a> for direct control of elements,
      layout, and events.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/dioxus/">Dioxus</a> for reactive components and signals.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="guides">Guides</h2>
  <ul class="overview-links">
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/elements/">Elements and text</a> covers layout, editing,
      lists, and tables.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/ssh/">SSH</a> serves an interface to remote clients.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/packages/">Formatting and keymaps</a> covers optional
      features and key bindings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/architecture/">Architecture</a> explains ownership and
      crate boundaries.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
